parameters.text:
=Create a comprehensive and unified Project Outline and Blueprint for the service: "{{ $json.project.name }}".

Sector: {{ $json.project.sector }}
Geography: {{ $json.project.geo }}
Client: {{ $json.project.client }}
Audience: {{ $json.project.audience }}
Description: {{ $json.project.desc }}
Standards: {{ $json.project.standards }}
Price/Budget: {{ $json.project.price }}
Duration: {{ $json.project.duration }}
Language: {{ $json.project.lang }}

Define the following keys in a clean, professional JSON structure:
1. projectTitle: The official unified title
2. executiveObjective: 2-3 sentences of the primary objective
3. coreMethodologies: An array of 3-4 specific standards/methodologies to use throughout the documents
4. primaryLocation: Location context
5. mainStakeholders: An array of key stakeholders (names/roles) to mention across documents
6. keyMilestones: An array of milestones with durations
7. priceSummary: Financial breakdown details

Provide only a valid raw JSON object. Do not wrap in markdown code blocks.

parameters.jsCode:
// Extract the blueprint JSON generated in the previous step
const rawBlueprint = $node["Generate Blueprint Plan"].json.text;
let blueprintObj = {};
try {
  blueprintObj = JSON.parse(rawBlueprint.replace(/```json|```/g, '').trim());
} catch (e) {
  // Fallback if parsing fails
  blueprintObj = { error: "Failed to parse blueprint", raw: rawBlueprint };
}

// We need to pass the list of docs as separate items to loop over them
const inputData = $node["Parse Inputs"].json;
const docs = inputData.docs;
const project = inputData.project;

return docs.map((doc, index) => {
  return {
    json: {
      index: index,
      totalDocs: docs.length,
      doc: doc,
      project: project,
      blueprint: blueprintObj
    }
  };
});

parameters.text:
=Generate a comprehensive, client-ready consulting document for the target output: "{{ $json.doc.name }}" (Category: {{ $json.doc.cat }}).

Use this unified Project Blueprint to ensure absolute consistency across names, numbers, objectives, and methodologies:
- Project Title: {{ $json.blueprint.projectTitle }}
- Objective: {{ $json.blueprint.executiveObjective }}
- Location Context: {{ $json.blueprint.primaryLocation }}
- Stakeholders: {{ JSON.stringify($json.blueprint.mainStakeholders) }}
- Key Milestones: {{ JSON.stringify($json.blueprint.keyMilestones) }}
- Budget Breakdown: {{ JSON.stringify($json.blueprint.priceSummary) }}
- Standard Methodologies: {{ JSON.stringify($json.blueprint.coreMethodologies) }}

Document Description / Target Objective:
{{ $json.project.desc }}

Output Directives:
1. Output format must be strictly clean Markdown.
2. Write in the target language: {{ $json.project.lang }}.
3. Be thorough, detailed, and professional (aim for 1500+ words). Do not use summary statements or placeholders.
4. Use structured headings, markdown tables, list items, and/or Mermaid.js diagrams to outline flowcharts if applicable.
5. Tone: Senior McKinsey/BCG management consultant.

parameters.jsCode:
const docText = $node["Generate Document Content"].json.text;
const docInfo = $json.doc;
const idx = $json.index + 1;
const padIdx = String(idx).padStart(2, '0');

// Clean filename
const safeName = docInfo.name.replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9]/g, '_');
const catFolder = docInfo.cat.toUpperCase();
const fileName = `${catFolder}/${padIdx}_${safeName}.md`;

const binaryData = Buffer.from(docText, 'utf-8');

return {
  json: {
    fileName: fileName,
    docId: docInfo.id,
    docName: docInfo.name
  },
  binary: {
    data: {
      data: binaryData.toString('base64'),
      mimeType: 'text/markdown',
      fileName: fileName
    }
  }
};
